  ⚠ Start a git repository in /srv/files-example and take it over?              
                                                                                
  Yes looks at the folder once more and makes the changes listed below only if  
  its list is unchanged. The folder belongs to the engine rootless:alice.       
  Containers of these stacks already run, so deploying would create duplicate   
  containers and take their ports twice. qhost only warns.                      
                                                                                
    folder: /srv/files-example                                                  
    case: files (files without a repository; a first commit takes the listed    
    files)                                                                      
    engine: rootless:alice                                                      
    owner: root, group: root, mode: 0755                                        
    the service can write it: no                                                
    permissions are set: yes                                                    
                                                                                
  Files of the first commit (2)                                                 
    demo/.env                                                                   
    demo/compose.yaml                                                           
                                                                                
  Left out (2), not needed by the stacks, kept out of git by .gitignore         
